---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lang = 'en';
---

<Layout lang={lang}>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  
  <main class="flex-1">
    {/* Hero */}
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-24 sm:py-32">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="text-center">
          <h1 class="font-mono text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-mono-50 sm:text-6xl">
            Roamy
          </h1>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-mono-300">
            Your terminal, from anywhere.
          </p>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base text-mono-500">
            An open-source session runtime that lets you access terminal sessions from your phone, browser, or any device &mdash; with end-to-end encryption and multi-device support.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-10 flex justify-center gap-4">
            <a
              href="https://github.com/RoamyDev"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="rounded-full border border-mono-600 bg-mono-900 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-mono-200 transition-colors hover:border-mono-400 hover:text-mono-50"
            >
              GitHub &rarr;
            </a>
            <span class="rounded-full border border-mono-800 bg-mono-950 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-mono-500">
              Work in Progress — actively developing
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* What is Roamy */}
    <section class="border-t border-mono-800/50 py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-mono-50">The Problem</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400 leading-relaxed">
            You SSH into a remote machine, start a long-running AI agent, then need to check on it from your phone. Or you're deep in a lazygit session and want to approve a merge from a mobile-friendly UI instead of squinting at raw terminal output.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400 leading-relaxed">
            Today's tools make you choose: either a full terminal with tiny text on mobile, or give up and wait until you're back at your desk. There's no middle ground.
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-12 font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-mono-50">The Approach</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400 leading-relaxed">
            Roamy is a <strong class="text-mono-200">session runtime</strong> that sits between your terminal and your devices. It captures terminal output, streams it over WebSocket, and &mdash; with an extensible adapter system &mdash; can parse the screen to understand <em>what program is running</em> and <em>what state it's in</em>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400 leading-relaxed">
            Clients can render touch-friendly interfaces for recognized programs, while always falling back to the raw terminal for everything else. All traffic between runtime and clients is end-to-end encrypted.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* Features */}
    <section class="border-t border-mono-800/50 py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="text-center font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-mono-50">Core Capabilities</h2>
        <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-5xl gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-medium text-mono-100">Cross-Platform Clients</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mono-400">
              Native desktop, web, and iOS clients &mdash; access your terminal from any device, anytime. Each client is optimized for its platform.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-medium text-mono-100">End-to-End Encrypted</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mono-400">
              All terminal traffic between runtime and clients is encrypted end-to-end. Your data never passes through our servers in plaintext.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-medium text-mono-100">Self-Hosted</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mono-400">
              Run it on your own infrastructure. No data routes through our servers &mdash; you control everything. Deploy behind your firewall, on-prem, or in the cloud.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-medium text-mono-100">Open Source Core</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mono-400">
              Protocol, runtime, and web client are Apache 2.0. Fully usable as a standalone remote terminal system. Audit, fork, contribute.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-medium text-mono-100">Remote Sessions</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mono-400">
              Persistent terminal sessions. Attach, detach, and reconnect from any device without losing state. Built on Rust for performance and reliability.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* Open Source */}
    <section class="border-t border-mono-800/50 py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-mono-50">Open Source</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400">
            The core system is open source under Apache 2.0. We are actively developing &mdash; star the repos to follow progress!
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 space-y-3">
            <a href="https://github.com/RoamyDev/roamy-protocol" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 px-5 py-3 transition-colors hover:border-mono-600">
              <div>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-mono-100">roamy-protocol</span>
                <span class="ml-3 text-sm text-mono-500">Protobuf wire protocol definitions</span>
              </div>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-mono-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-400">Apache 2.0</span>
            </a>
            <a href="https://github.com/RoamyDev/roamy-runtime" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 px-5 py-3 transition-colors hover:border-mono-600">
              <div>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-mono-100">roamy-runtime</span>
                <span class="ml-3 text-sm text-mono-500">Session daemon + core runtime</span>
              </div>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-mono-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-400">Apache 2.0</span>
            </a>
            <a href="https://github.com/RoamyDev/roamy-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/30 px-5 py-3 transition-colors hover:border-mono-600">
              <div>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-mono-100">roamy-web</span>
                <span class="ml-3 text-sm text-mono-500">Browser terminal client</span>
              </div>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-mono-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-400">Apache 2.0</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
